Preview how a time phrase resolves before using it.

Every flag that takes a time (`snooze --until`, `send --at`, `send --remind-after`, `remind --when`, `send-time --at`) reads the same phrases, in local time with your snooze hours: `tomorrow`, `tonight`, `weekend`, `fri`, `fri 3`, `tue 9am`, `next week`, `next month`, `3 oct 5pm`, `in 2h`, `3d`, `eod`, `noon`, RFC3339. Ambiguous phrases list every reading; the first is what a flag uses.

Usage: mxr time [OPTIONS] <PHRASE>...

Arguments:
  <PHRASE>...
          The phrase to resolve, such as "fri 3" or "in 2d"

Options:
      --now <RFC3339>
          Resolve relative to this RFC3339 instant instead of now

      --format <FORMAT>
          [possible values: table, json, jsonl, csv, ids]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
